# A CANDIDATE: PARKING WHEN TOLD (parking step 2, the engine part;
# docs/notes/parking-step-2.md §6 - its second cut, ACCEPTED for staging by
# the architecture session, 2026-11-25). engine-stream.series, line for line,
# then:
#   0023  the backend's Free parks a model that can park; a LoadModel with the
#         options of its load brings it back ("Model already loaded", byte for
#         byte); a request brings it back by itself and never parks; Status
#         says where the weights are; one answer for a full device
#         (RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED "no_room_on_device: ..."), and a failure never
#         answered as a refusal.
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-park.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# ANOTHER ENGINE: a build and every gate again - and what changes for EVERY
# model the day it runs is a table in the note, for the gate to cover.
# NO MODEL FILE may set GGML_SYCL_PARKABLE=1 before the SERVER part is live:
# today's LocalAI calls Free before it stops a process, so such a model's
# every stop would first copy its weights to the host (a test holds every
# staged model file to it). Its rows are on COPIES (§6):
#   python3 -I tools/measure/park_told.py cycles ADDR <model> -n 20 --return request
